WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:14.466
Hi! In visual text comprehension, you get a poster, an advertisement or a flyer, and answer some multiple-choice questions. Let's learn how to find the answers quickly and accurately.

2
00:00:14.616 --> 00:00:22.530
Step one: look at the big heading and pictures to see what it's about. This poster is for the Sunny Park Green Fair.

3
00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:33.306
Step two: think about the purpose. Is it to inform, to persuade, or to invite? Free entry with an exclamation mark is trying to get people to come.

4
00:00:33.456 --> 00:00:41.946
Step three: notice special conditions. Bring your own bag and get a free plant. You only get the plant if you bring a bag.

5
00:00:42.096 --> 00:00:52.122
And the small print! After the star, it says you must sign up for workshops at the info booth. Small print often hides answers.

6
00:00:52.272 --> 00:00:58.026
Read the question first so you know what to look for, then find the key words in the poster.

7
00:00:58.176 --> 00:01:02.874
Bold words, big words, colours and stars are all important.

8
00:01:03.024 --> 00:01:09.978
Check every option against the text. Don't choose from memory or guesswork.

9
00:01:10.128 --> 00:01:15.378
Watch out! Some pupils see the word free and think everything is free.

10
00:01:15.528 --> 00:01:21.402
The poster says entry is free and the plant is free, but only if you bring your own bag.

11
00:01:21.552 --> 00:01:27.666
So compare the conditions in each option with the poster, word by word.

12
00:01:27.816 --> 00:01:40.218
Your turn! What is the main purpose of the poster: to sell bags, to invite people to a fair, or to teach about plants? Pause and think.

13
00:01:40.368 --> 00:01:46.770
The answer is B: to invite people to the fair. Did you get it right?

14
00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:54.906
Another one! How can you get a free plant? Pause and think.

15
00:01:55.056 --> 00:02:00.882
The answer is: bring your own bag. Did you get it right?

16
00:02:01.032 --> 00:02:12.282
Here's another! The fair runs from 9 am to 1 pm. How many hours is it open? Pause and think.

17
00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:17.634
The answer is four hours. Did you get it right?

18
00:02:17.784 --> 00:02:26.346
One more! What must you do before joining a workshop? Pause and think.

19
00:02:26.496 --> 00:02:35.370
The answer is: sign up at the info booth. It's hidden in the small print after the star. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:43.578
And another! Do you have to pay to enter the fair? Pause and think.

21
00:02:43.728 --> 00:02:54.090
The answer is no. The poster says free entry. But to get a free plant, you still need to bring your own bag. Did you get it right?

22
00:02:54.240 --> 00:03:06.066
Remember: look at the heading and pictures, think about the purpose, then read each question and find the key words in the text. Watch out for conditions, small print and stars.

23
00:03:06.216 --> 00:03:12.258
Next time you see a poster, ask yourself: what does it want me to do?

